=== buffer-squeeze test on data/q5_iid_b15.txt (mode iid) ===
For each decade: Aitken on every usable buffer, versus Aitken on only
the three buffers sitting 3, 4 and 5 decades above the decade's top,
which is all the deepest decade of this run has.

        decade  all buffers  headroom 3-5  difference
  1e5->1e6              0.5906        0.5899     -0.0007
  1e6->1e7              0.6154        0.6145     -0.0009
  1e7->1e8              0.6315        0.6309     -0.0006
  1e8->1e9              0.6422        0.6422     -0.0000
  1e9->1e10             0.6475        0.6475     +0.0000

A positive difference means the squeezed extrapolation over-reads, so
the deep decades of this run carry that much upward extrapolation error
on top of their bootstrap band.
